From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: AVR on DPU 8 and split DSI

0107 sets up the INTF's AVR on DPU 9 and later only. DPU 8 has the same
block at the same offsets: Qualcomm's SM8450 driver runs Qsync on it for
video mode panels.

A split display halves each INTF's horizontal timings but kept the full
pixel clock, so AVR's longest frame came out twice as long as the panel's
floor. Halve the clock with them.

The AYANEO Pocket VERT (SM8475, DPU 8, two DSI links) runs variable refresh
through both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -355,6 +355,7 @@ static void dpu_encoder_phys_vid_setup_t
 		mode.hsync_start >>= 1;
 		mode.hsync_end >>= 1;
 		mode.hskew >>= 1;
+		mode.clock >>= 1;
 
 		DPU_DEBUG_VIDENC(phys_enc,
 			"split_role %d, halve horizontal %d %d %d %d %d\n",
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_intf.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_intf.c
@@ -708,7 +708,7 @@ struct dpu_hw_intf *dpu_hw_intf_init(str
 	if (mdss_rev->core_major_ver >= 7)
 		c->ops.program_intf_cmd_cfg = dpu_hw_intf_program_intf_cmd_cfg;
 
-	if (mdss_rev->core_major_ver >= 9 && cfg->type == INTF_DSI) {
+	if (mdss_rev->core_major_ver >= 8 && cfg->type == INTF_DSI) {
 		c->ops.setup_avr = dpu_hw_intf_setup_avr;
 		c->ops.enable_avr = dpu_hw_intf_enable_avr;
 		c->ops.avr_trigger = dpu_hw_intf_avr_trigger;
